          "end": 176.85,
          "en": "query with eloquent or Warren Builder sorry, query builder, those queries will run in other databases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 177.66,
          "en": "as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 180.24,
          "en": "Other supported databases to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 180.24,
          "end": 186.45,
          "en": "So Laravel supports multiple databases, you know, multiple multiple types of databases like MySQL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.48,
          "end": 188.85,
          "en": "Postgres, SQLite, etc..",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 195.42,
          "en": "So suppose currently you are using MySQL and in future you want to upgrade it or shift to Postgres.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 203.28,
          "en": "Suppose in the time when you will shift to Postgres, you don't have to change any kind of query because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 203.28,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "you used either a query builder or elegant ORM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 207.09,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "Now Laravel will by default convert your queries and work in Postgres without any kind of issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "But if you had used any kind of raw queries and you write the raw queries, it won't work because your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "database is totally changed and all the databases have their own syntax syntax a little bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "So your application will break.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 236.67000000000002,
          "en": "So that's why we always use either a query builder and or eloquent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 243.51,
          "en": "Now eloquent is most of the time recommended, but also we use Query Builder as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 243.6,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "Uh, most of the time when we have lots of lots of data in our database, we want to fetch and manipulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 249.93,
          "en": "In that time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 249.93,
          "end": 255.48,
          "en": "Query builder is really handy because it is, uh, more faster than eloquent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 255.48,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "But when we are working with normal data, we use eloquent because eloquent is more flexible and human",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 262.11,
          "en": "readable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 262.14,
          "end": 269.52,
          "en": "You can run a write a small query for big, uh, SQL syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 275.01,
          "en": "We'll be talking about this later on as we'll be working with the, uh, Eloquent Builder right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 275.01,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "So let's talk about the eloquent builder there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "Uh, so I already told you some benefits of using Eloquent and Query builder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 283.05,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "Right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 287.82,
          "en": "So I hope you got the idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 287.82,
          "end": 295.03,
          "en": "So that means when we write our queries via Query Builder, it will run in other databases as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 295.03,
          "end": 300.04,
          "en": "then also it will protect us from exercise injections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
